WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.090
Pre-planning is the name of the game in the
entertainment industry.

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.120
More often than not, video games get stamped
with release dates long before they're ready

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:13.730
to hit the shelves, and 2018's release calendar
is already jam-packed with sensational new

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:14.730
titles.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.680
Here are the games that will blow everyone
away in 2018.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.450
Far Cry 5

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:26.090
The latest installment in Ubisoft's first-person
shooter franchise, Far Cry 5 is set in fictional

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:30.410
Hope County, Montana in a small town that's
seems like a slice of perfection.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:34.940
Stare a little longer, though, and the violence,
racial tensions, and a faith-obsessed sect

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.399
emerge from the shadows.

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:41.469
At the bloody heart of Far Cry 5 is that very
band of believers, hell bent on seizing a

00:00:41.469 --> 00:00:46.769
chunk of the American midwest and transforming
its residents into god-fearing faithfuls.

00:00:46.769 --> 00:00:51.160
Early reactions to Far Cry 5 have all seemed
to echo the same sentiment: from the game's

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:56.100
captivating landscape to its "uncanny ability
to anticipate modern cultural and political

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.829
trends," it simply doesn't get more raw than
Far Cry 5.

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:03.059
Mark your calendar for when it releases on
February 27.

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:04.199
2018.

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:06.869
Bloodstained: Ritual of the Night

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:11.680
Almost entirely crowdfunded, Bloodstained:
Ritual of the Night is currently in development

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.780
with former Castlevania head honcho Koji Igarashi.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:19.520
Unsurprisingly, this trippy side-scrolling
platformer has been marketed as a spiritual

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.640
successor to the dark-fantasy-themed game
series, but will feature gameplay that post-dates

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.820
1997's Symphony of the Night.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:31.030
You'll traverse the monster-filled world as
Miriam, a young orphan plagued by a curse

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:33.619
that slowly turns her skin to crystal.

00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:37.939
Surpassing its Kickstarter goal with ease,
Igarashi's return to form looks like it'll

00:01:37.939 --> 00:01:42.799
shine in its two-and-a-half dimensions — and
knock your socks off in the process.

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:48.340
Be prepared to buy the game in March 2018
on a variety of system platforms.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.159
Monster Hunter: World

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:55.250
Monster Hunter is a sensation in the gaming
world, selling over 40 million games since

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.869
the franchise's debut in 2004.

00:01:57.869 --> 00:02:01.729
And yet the series has struggled to gain traction
outside of Japan.

00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:04.149
Monster Hunter: World aims to fix that.

00:02:04.149 --> 00:02:06.020
It says as much right in the title.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:10.229
Like before, hunters prepare in town before
embarking on excursions into the wilderness,

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:14.580
where they'll need to adhere to carefully
planned strategies in order to take down the

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.860
game's massive beasts.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.290
But Capcom, the game's publisher, is making
some changes, too.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:23.650
Instead of tromping through a series of smaller,
walled-off areas, Monster Hunter: World takes

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.409
place in an open and dynamic environment.

00:02:26.409 --> 00:02:28.400
That's right: no loading screens.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.600
The series' notoriously deep learning curve
has also been softened, and the interface

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.040
has been streamlined to accommodate new players.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.430
As executive director Kaname Fujioka explained
it: "The grammar of games in the West is evolving.

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:45.159
And being able to say 'We speak your language'
is a great chance to get more people on board."

00:02:45.159 --> 00:02:50.170
This is a title we're definitely looking forward
to in early 2018.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.420
God of War

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.599
Kratos is back, but this isn't your father's
God of War.

00:02:55.599 --> 00:03:00.670
Sure, 2018's installment in the signature
PlayStation franchise will be just as gloriously

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:06.370
violent as ever, and yes, the demigod in the
face paint once again plays God of War's hero

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.939
— but that's where the similarities end.

00:03:08.939 --> 00:03:13.510
Instead of the sun-drenched Mediterranean,
this new God of War takes the action to snowy

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:17.460
Scandinavia, pitting our hero against characters
from Norse mythology.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.540
Instead of the over-the-top, pulp vibe that
characterized the original games, God of War

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.690
has a slower, more serious tone.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:27.489
This time, Kratos is joined on his quest by
his son, Atreus.

00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:28.489
That changes everything.

00:03:28.489 --> 00:03:33.720
Not only does Atreus help his old man during
combat, but God of War devotees know Kratos'

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:38.640
need for vengeance began when Ares tricked
the warrior into killing his first family.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:43.220
Director Cory Barlog says that Atreus is "the
humanity that Kratos has lost [...] He's that

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:47.330
mirror that is reminding him that there's
a different way — a way he might have forgotten

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:48.330
long ago."

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:52.390
But before you start worrying that God of
War trades action for introspection, rest

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:56.879
assured that underneath the mature storyline
is a brutal and exciting adventure in the

00:03:56.879 --> 00:04:00.980
classic God of War style, albeit with a more
modern flavor.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:05.510
Instead of fixed camera angles and linear
solutions to problems, God of War gives players

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:09.400
the tools they need to proceed, then lets
them find the best solution to the game's

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.470
obstacles.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:15.290
The tone might be new, but at its core God
of War will still be the god-murdering simulator

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:20.109
we've all come to know and love — like its
hero, it's just grown up a little.

00:04:20.109 --> 00:04:22.800
Look for it early 2018.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.870
System Shock

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:29.260
Completely revamped from the 1994 original,
this System Shock remake takes no prisoners.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:33.830
Portland-based developer Night Dive Studios
has enlisted a dazzling team of industry veterans

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:38.660
to craft a high-powered new game that centers
around a keenly resourceful hacker who's taken

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:42.210
prisoner by a money-hungry TriOptimum executive
— basically a scarier, cyberpunk version

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.210
of a Wall Street Banker.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:46.990
2018's System Shock catapults players into
the post-apocalyptic landscape of Citadel

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:52.960
Station — which is now inhabited by brainless
robots, corrupt cyborgs, and grotesquely mutilated

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:58.090
creatures, all of which are engineered to
obey the merciless A.I. known as SHODAN.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:02.500
And if that wasn't enough, Night Dive Studios
promises the world of System Shock has "never

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.470
been more immersive or terrifying" than in
the upcoming reboot.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:11.280
We're excited to find out if that's true in
the second quarter of 2018.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.060
Crackdown 3

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:17.610
Crackdown 3 was originally supposed to come
out in 2016, and then it was pushed back to

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.830
November 7, 2017.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:23.250
Now the open-world adventure is set for spring
2018.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:25.360
Will the third time be the charm?

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:29.820
Microsoft regrets the delays, and admits it
revealed Crackdown 3 a few years too early.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:32.050
Hopefully, the finished product will be worth
the wait.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:36.449
As in previous installments, Crackdown 3 lets
you control a super-powered agent who hunts

00:05:36.449 --> 00:05:41.800
down criminals, but the game's real draw is
that you can destroy anything and everything.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:42.889
Literally.

00:05:42.889 --> 00:05:46.750
By offloading some of the game's processing
into the cloud, Crackdown 3 features fully

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:50.530
destructible environments — at least in
multiplayer — setting the stage for some

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:51.780
truly epic battles.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.610
If you can see it, you can wreck it.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:58.300
Now that developer Sumo Digital has the the
extra time it needs to make sure Crackdown

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:02.260
3 shines, the game could represent a major
breakthrough in terms of technology as well

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.020
as open-world warfare.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:09.819
Besides, blowing stuff up is fun, and Crackdown
3 explodes things real good.

00:06:09.819 --> 00:06:11.250
That's good enough for us.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.930
"Forget dropping bombs!

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.780
You're dropping BUILDINGS!

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.800
HAHAHA!"

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:19.810
Red Dead Redemption 2

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:24.530
Although there's a "two" tacked onto the end
of its title, Red Dead Redemption 2 is actually

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:28.789
the third installment in the action-adventure
franchise, and the first built from the ground

00:06:28.789 --> 00:06:33.500
up, eight years after Red Dead Redemption
and 12 years after the original Red Dead Revolver.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.990
The follow-up takes vintage Americana vibes
and atmospheric inspiration from its predecessors

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:42.539
to bring forth an "outlaw epic" featuring
plenty of gun-slinging cowboys and roughed-up

00:06:42.539 --> 00:06:43.539
rebels.

00:06:43.539 --> 00:06:47.860
We'll have to hold out a bit longer than originally
planned to get our hands on Red Dead Redemption

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:53.060
and its cast of scruffy characters, but considering
the game's near-limitless landscape and fierce

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:56.080
narrative, the days spent waiting may well
be worth it.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.470
Look for this sequel in spring 2018.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:00.729
Spider-Man

00:07:00.729 --> 00:07:05.800
In Insomniac's upcoming PlayStation 4 exclusive,
players will slip into a new version of Peter

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:10.440
Parker's iconic red and blue suit and guide
the wallcrawler through the island of Manhattan

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:15.440
on a map that's reportedly four times bigger
than the one in the developer's last open-world

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:17.690
game, Sunset Overdrive.

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:21.389
Players will swing between buildings, take
on Spidey's foes, and use all the tricks and

00:07:21.389 --> 00:07:25.190
tools at Peter's disposal to rescue civilians
and save the day.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:30.819
Judging by the game's extended E3 2017 demo,
Insomniac has lifted the best parts of recent

00:07:30.819 --> 00:07:34.849
superhero games and combined them into something
both new and familiar.

00:07:34.849 --> 00:07:39.379
Combat looks like it's inspired by Batman:
Arkham City, allowing players to sneak and

00:07:39.379 --> 00:07:44.241
swing among the rafters and take down thugs
with various attacks, or drop down to street

00:07:44.241 --> 00:07:46.979
level to engage in some rhythm-driven fisticuffs.

00:07:46.979 --> 00:07:49.910
But the cool stuff for Spidey fans doesn't
end there.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:53.569
It looks like the developers are including
some of the newest additions to the Spider-Man

00:07:53.569 --> 00:07:54.569
universe.

00:07:54.569 --> 00:07:59.270
Mr. Negative, a modern take on Dr. Jekyll
and Mr. Hyde, plays a prominent role.

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:03.300
Insomniac also confirms that classic Spidey
villains will surface — the Kingpin briefly

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.160
appeared in Sony's demo.

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:09.150
All in all, this is a Spider-Man that embraces
everything that makes the franchise great,

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:11.909
retro, modern, or in between.

00:08:11.909 --> 00:08:16.250
Spider-Man is set for release in the first
half of 2018.

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:17.770
Anthem

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:21.530
BioWare isn't the first developer you'd expect
to make an open-world multiplayer shooter

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:26.430
— until now, the studio has stuck almost
exclusively to role-playing games, with classics

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:31.819
like Baldur's Gate, Knights of the Old Republic,
Mass Effect, and Dragon Age.

00:08:31.819 --> 00:08:36.220
But if the game's E3 trailer is anything like
the final product, the veteran studio will

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:38.010
knock everyone's socks off.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:41.710
Who hasn't wanted to fly around and kick butt
with a jetpack?

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:44.900
Anthem looks like it'll be worth it for that
gameplay hook alone.

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:48.960
Players join the ranks of the Freelancers,
intrepid explorers who journey into the wilderness

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.520
to fight vicious beasts and gather loot.

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:55.670
Players can team up to tackle particularly
tough challenges in Anthem's sprawling shared

00:08:55.670 --> 00:09:00.190
world, assuming different classes like the
all-purpose Ranger or the tank-like Colossus,

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:02.640
each of which plays a different role in battle.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:06.930
Massive "Shaper Storms" promise to shake up
Anthem with their "world-altering" consequences,

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:11.720
while players can zoom using the jetpacks
built into their Javelin exosuits, flying

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:16.030
across the map or taking to the air to snipe
opponents on the ground.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:19.860
Maybe a little of BioWare's storytelling magic
will rub off on Anthem, too.

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:24.570
Drew Karpyshyn, lead writer on the first two
Mass Effect games is penning Anthem's story.

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:28.272
Hunting for loot in games is always great,
but having a good reason to hunt for it is

00:09:28.272 --> 00:09:29.272
even better.

00:09:29.272 --> 00:09:33.771
If BioWare can fuse a strong narrative with
Destiny's addictive gameplay loop, Anthem

00:09:33.771 --> 00:09:36.830
might ending up being very, very hard to put
down.

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:38.860
Look for it Fall 2018.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:41.650
Detroit: Become Human

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:46.120
David Cage's games, which skirt the line between
point-and-click adventure and interactive

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:47.820
movie, aren't for everyone.

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:52.140
Heavy Rain received positive reviews on release,
but some of the game's odder features haven't

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:53.260
aged quite as well.

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:57.470
Cage's follow up, Beyond: Two Souls, looked
and sounded great, but didn't include much

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.170
in the way of interactivity.

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:02.900
But every time Cage and the team at Quantic
Dream put out a new game, the formula gets

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:07.350
a little more complex — and Detroit: Become
Human might be where they get the balance

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:10.130
between story and action just right.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:14.000
Like Cage's other games, Detroit lets players
guide multiple characters through a branching

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:17.100
storyline that changes based on the user's
decisions.

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:19.730
As in Heavy Rain, death isn't the end, either.

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:24.050
If one character dies, the story continues,
and adapts to that person's absence.

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:28.500
Three androids — Kara, Connor, and Markus
— serve as our guides into a near-future

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:32.300
setting where artificial lifeforms struggle
to find their place in the world.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:36.120
With the player's help, they'll find a way
to settle peacefully alongside humanity, take

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:40.170
to the streets in a full-fledged revolution,
or something in between.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:42.160
Just don't expect any easy answers.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:45.340
Cage says: "There is no big message to humanity
in this game.

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:49.070
[...] It's just interesting questions that
may resonate with your own personal values

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:52.500
and just confront you with the consequences
[of your] actions."

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:57.190
Detroit: Become Human is set for release in
2018, although as of this video it doesn't

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:59.810
have an official release date.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:01.390
Kingdom Hearts 3

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.450
At long last, it's coming.

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:07.750
Kingdom Hearts 2, the last numbered entry
in this Final Fantasy and Disney mashup, came

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:13.670
out way back in 2005, and fans have been waiting
for a proper follow-up ever since.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.440
And now we're finally getting it.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:20.260
As before, series hero Sora and his pals will
travel to lands based on popular Disney properties

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:22.380
while fighting the evil Heartless.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.750
Kingdom Hearts 3 doubles down on the Disney,
too.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:29.070
Sora can unleash powerful summon attacks based
on Disneyland and Disney World attractions,

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:33.320
while the new settings take full advantage
of Disney's expanded corporate portfolio.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:37.750
That's right: both Pixar and even Marvel characters
are set to make their Kingdom Hearts debut.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:40.490
Look for it in 2018.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.050
The Last Night

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:46.460
It's not often that an indie game threatens
to steal an entire E3 press conference, but

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:50.390
in 2017, The Last Night almost did just that.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:54.890
By fusing a Blade Runner-esque environment
with modern cinematic effects and flashy pixel

00:11:54.890 --> 00:12:00.240
art, The Last Night oozes style, and almost
brought Microsoft's presentation to a standstill.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:05.010
The Last Night started as small prototype
developed during 2014's Cyberpunk Jam, and

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:09.800
designer Tim Soret only decided to flesh out
the game into a fully-fledged project after

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.850
it won the event's top prize.

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:16.910
As far as the actual gameplay goes, Soret
describes The Last Night as a "cinematic adventure

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:21.680
game," while publisher Raw Fury says it'll
feature "a diverse, inclusive cast of complex

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:25.510
characters to interact with through meaningful,
branching dialogue."

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:30.120
Hopefully The Last World will be a game everyone
can enjoy when it arrives on the Xbox One

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:33.640
and Windows PC in 2018.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:34.800
Death Stranding

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:40.470
The infamously ambiguous Death Stranding is
a definite possibility for release in 2018,

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:45.210
as its creator Hideo Kojima has given more
than a few hints that point to a debut sometime

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:46.410
next year.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:51.330
During the 2016 Tokyo Game Show, Kojima stated,
"It will be out before the Olympics.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:55.690
[...] To go a little further, there is a movie
called Akira, and it will be out before the

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:57.580
year in which Akira is set."

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:02.970
The former references the 2020 Tokyo Games,
the latter the year 2019.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:07.720
Whether or not it actually arrives in 2018,
Death Stranding has already piqued many gamers'

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:08.720
interest.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:12.830
From the minute we saw a CGI Norman Reedus
cradling a baby on a deserted beach in the

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:15.060
middle of nowhere, we were hooked.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:19.230
Since then, it's been revealed that Hannibal
actor Mads Mikkelsen and director Guillermo

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:24.750
del Toro have joined the project, which blends
open-world gameplay with unique elements and

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:26.020
an intricate plot.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:31.490
Color us excited and counting down the days
until this hopeful 2018 release.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:32.620
Code Vein

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:37.290
When gamers got their first glimpse of Code
Vein, few knew what to make of it.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:42.130
From the team behind the sci-fi action-adventure
series God Eater, Code Vein packs some serious

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:47.170
vampire heat, throwing players into a dystopian
dungeon to play as a blood-sucking Revenant

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:51.030
with a network of supernatural powers laid
out just beneath his thumb.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:55.690
Or, rather, behind his teeth, as bearing down
on some fresh flesh grants him new unique

00:13:55.690 --> 00:14:00.870
abilities — ones players can put to the
test throughout Code Vein's massive, interconnected

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:01.870
world.

